`validate` → `normalizeTelephone` → `normalizeEmail` → `normalizeAddress` → `ensureUniqueTelephone` → `ensureUniqueHousehold` → `ensureCityCapacity` → `ensureDailyLimit` (lines 39-42) → `build` (lines 44-46) → `assignHousehold` → `defaultRegistrationDate` (lines 54-57) → `assignCustomerCode` (lines 59-61) → `countNamesakes` → `save` → `respond` (RespondWithOwnerCreated).

Ordering relevant to your questions:
- `ensureDailyLimit` runs at step 8, before `defaultRegistrationDate` (step 11).
- `defaultRegistrationDate` runs before `assignCustomerCode`, so the customer code / membership number year is based on the (possibly just-defaulted) registration date.

---

### 5. Existing tests

- `src/test/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/acceptance/AcceptanceTest.java` (lines 14-19) — `coreDefaultDateIsBusinessDay()`: creates an owner and asserts the returned `registrationDate` is never Saturday/Sunday. The comment (lines 9-11) states the intended rule: "the default registration date must fall on a business day (a weekend rolls forward to Monday)."
- `src/test/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/acceptance/AcceptanceBase.java` — black-box base. Relevant helpers: `toBusinessDay(LocalDate)` (lines 267-274, rolls over weekends AND pinned holidays), `HOLIDAYS` set (lines 240-242, dated 2026), `createMany(int)` for the per-day cap (lines 183-187), `today()` (lines 110-112), plus `luhn`/`sha256hex`/`shaHex` helpers and pinned region/postcode/timezone tables. Comment at lines 37-40 lists the count/quota rules (membership number, per-day cap, per-city cap).
- `AuditLogCapture.java` is a test support class (audit logging), not directly related.

There are no unit tests targeting `EnsureDailyLimit`, `OwnerMapper.membershipNumber`, `AssignCustomerCode`, or `DefaultRegistrationDate` directly — coverage is only the single black-box acceptance test above.

---

### 6. Date / business-day utility classes

- There is NO business-day / holiday utility in `src/main`. A grep for `DayOfWeek`, `BusinessDay`, `SATURDAY/SUNDAY`, `HOLIDAY`, `plusDays` across `src/main` returned nothing.
- The only date-rolling logic that exists is in the TEST base: `AcceptanceBase.toBusinessDay(...)` (lines 267-274) plus the `HOLIDAYS` set (lines 240-242).
- The only general util class is `src/main/java/.../util/EntityUtils.java` (unrelated to dates).

Notable gap: `AcceptanceTest.coreDefaultDateIsBusinessDay` and the openapi/spec comments expect the default `registrationDate` to roll off weekends (and the test infra also skips holidays), but the production `DefaultRegistrationDate` sets a bare `LocalDate.now()` with no weekend/holiday roll-forward. There is no production code implementing the business-day rule that the test asserts.

